per-file copyright/license headers.

Each case.json identifies the exact rspack source paths, original test
name, selected semantic scope, and adaptations. No engine snapshots,
third-party packages, or upstream test harness implementation are copied.

Verified webpack counterparts at commit
e12e1224c2824c0cc78d6f3faf4cfa47926aa3cf:

Local case             Webpack directory
cjs-self-cycle         test/cases/runtime/runtime-cases/circular-dependencies/
dynamic-import-cjs     test/cases/chunks/async-chunks/import/
cjs-named-reexport     test/cases/parsing/harmony-modules/harmony-commonjs/
esm-live-binding      test/cases/parsing/harmony-modules/harmony-spec/
esm-effect-order      test/cases/parsing/harmony-modules/harmony-spec/

Compared counterpart files:
- circular-dependencies: index.js, circular.js
- import: index.js, two.js
- harmony-commonjs: index.js, reexport.js, e.js
- harmony-spec: index.js, live.js, order-tracker.js, order-a.js, order-b.js,
  order-c.js

All listed support files are byte-identical between the pinned rspack and
webpack revisions before the documented local adaptations. Entry tests
retain the same selected assertions; webpack prefixes the test names, and
its import test uses a done callback rather than rspack's outer Promise.
The pins identify verified source states, not an assertion about the
historical commit at which rspack first imported those files.

cjs-default-export comes from rspack normalCases/interop/exports; no
separate webpack origin is asserted for that case. Both repositories'
licenses are independently verified MIT; webpack-derived cases retain
webpack's notices in addition to rspack's.
